<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung, Daewoo consider Indonesia joint venture.</title>
<headline>Samsung, Daewoo consider Indonesia joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Samsung Display Devices Co said on Wednesday it is considering setting up a joint venture plant in Indonesia to make colour television components with Orion Electric Co Ltd.</p>
<p>A Samsung spokesman said Japan's Toshiba Corp is also seeking participation in the project, which is expected to put out 40 million shadow mask units annually for colour television sets.</p>
<p>Samsung Display is a unit of South Korea's Samsung Group. Orion Electric is a unit of Daewoo Group.</p>
</text>
